00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
dear friends  i thank the rrr team for this invitation  the european commission's union of  equality work provides particular  attention to intersectional minority  identities and the multiple  discrimination that persons belonging to  such groups often experience  of course this is also true for roma  lgbtiq persons indeed the commission has  firmly anchored these issues in the  reformed eu roma strategic framework and  the first eu lgbt iq equality strategy  since the beginning of my mandate i have  made sure that the commission implements  its equality strategies using  intersectionality  as a cross-cutting principle for  instance the eu-roma strategic framework  encourages an intersectional approach in  view of the fact that on occasions  discrimination on the grounds of ethnic  origin is compounded with discrimination  on other aspects of identity  it explicitly calls on the member states  to focus more on diversity among roma by  ensuring that national strategic  frameworks meet the specific needs of  different groups including the roma  lgbtiq community  i continue to work closely with member  states to foster acknowledgement that  discrimination is often compounded and  is an aspect that needs to be addressed  in the national strategies  and it must be addressed properly  but as you are likely to discuss today  we need to invest more in research and  targeted awareness raising about the  impact of multiple discrimination on  individuals  i am therefore very interested to hear  your recommendations on how we can best  reflect the challenges and concrete  policies and laws  close-up cooperation and open dialogue  with civil society organizations is an  essential part of our work and i always  make sure that civil society  organizations participate to the design  implementation and monitoring of our  equality policies  the commission will also continue to  provide funding to support civil society  organizations under the  2021-2027 citizens equality rights and  values program  supporting projects like yours is  crucial because they contribute greatly  to reaching our larger political goal of  a union of equality where we can ensure  safety integrity and equal opportunities  for all eu citizens

